<p><a href="https://williewilson2027.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website</a></p>
<p><a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Willie Wilson&#39;s campaign lists eleven priorities, each with a one-line goal and a short explanation. Tap here to read them on his site, then come back to comment.</a></p>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>The platform</h3>
<p>Costs: Cut taxes for working-class residents and businesses, cut red tape for business licenses, and push down the cost of groceries, housing, and insurance.</p>
<p>Schools: Students meet state standards before moving up a grade, and earn a trade certification before they graduate.</p>
<p>Pensions: Ask voters for a state constitutional amendment so Chicago can address its pension debt.</p>
<p>Also: Faster lead pipe removal, more neighborhood clinics and mental health care, transit that reaches every neighborhood, and keeping the Bears in Chicago.</p>
<h3>Next to the other candidates</h3>
<p>Only Wilson: Requiring a trade certification to graduate from high school.</p>
<p>Taxes: Holberg and Wilson promise lower taxes. Mendoza, Kelly, and Brewer say relief comes from a bigger tax base, and Carlisle proposes a new income tax tied to pension reform.</p>
<p>Pensions: Wilson wants a state constitutional amendment. Carlisle ties pension reform to a new income tax, and Cardenas calls for shared sacrifice from the city and its workers.</p>
